{{!
    @template local_reactions/pill

    A single emoji reaction pill showing an emoji and its count.
    Used as a partial by both reactions_bar and discussion_list_reactions.

    Context is a single button object from the buttons array.

    The pill is wrapped in a span so that `names` can hang a Bootstrap tooltip off an element that
    is never disabled — a disabled button receives no hover events, and read-only pills (discussion
    list, grading panel) are always disabled. `names` is empty unless the activity has "Show who
    reacted" turned on, and no tooltip is emitted then.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "shortcode": "thumbsup",
        "unicode": "\ud83d\udc4d",
        "count": 3,
        "hascount": true,
        "selected": true,
        "canreact": true,
        "names": "You, Jenny (Teacher), Andrew, and 2 others"
    }
}}
{{#hascount}}
    <span class="local-reactions-pill-wrapper"
        {{#names}}data-toggle="tooltip" data-placement="top" title="{{.}}"{{/names}}
    >
        <button
            type="button"
            class="local-reactions-pill{{#selected}} local-reactions-selected{{/selected}}"
            data-action="toggle-reaction"
            data-emoji="{{shortcode}}"
            data-count="{{count}}"
            aria-pressed="{{#selected}}true{{/selected}}{{^selected}}false{{/selected}}"
            aria-label="{{unicode}} {{count}}{{#names}}. {{.}}{{/names}}"
            {{^canreact}}disabled{{/canreact}}
        >
            <span class="local-reactions-emoji" aria-hidden="true">{{unicode}}</span>
            <span class="local-reactions-count" data-region="reaction-count">{{count}}</span>
        </button>
    </span>
{{/hascount}}
